# tally 2.1.8 R7 (item 9 of the follow-up): a refused line rests on the reads that refused it, so the with pin it
# took is listed under the refusal (p5: out on 2026-03-05 takes jar below 0), as the stored m1 vectors print. 2.1.8's
# first refcore (c13e6c8c) dropped it. The plan's c5s p5.
=== m.tally
model t
  tally 2
  on 2026-01-01
  start 2026-01-01
  end 2026-06-30

source s "s"
unit PLN: currency minor 0.01
kind savings: place PLN min 0
place jar: savings lives 2025-01-01..
place world: outside lives 1900-01-01..
input amt: money PLN
input wd: date
input dd: date

move out: transfers
  on wd
  leg cash from jar to world amount amt

move inn: transfers
  on dd
  leg cash from world to jar amount amt

version v
  cite s
  governs always
  known 2025-12-01
  amt = 100.00 PLN "s"
  wd = window(2026-03-05, 2026-03-10) "s"
  dd = 2026-03-07 "s"
  opening[jar] = 50.00 PLN at 2026-01-01 start "s"

ask p5: bal(jar, 2026-03-31) with wd = 2026-03-05
=== expect
p5: refused: RUN-PLACE jar is -50.00 PLN after the day's observations and plans of 2026-03-05
  pinned: wd = 2026-03-05
  cut 2026-01-01
